Exercise 28's superscript base, {(1-x^{2})}^{3/2}, is redundantly braced --
convert_script_base wraps any compound mrow base in {...} to keep a real
multi-atom expression like x+1 grouped, but here the base is already a
single parenthesized atom (the mfenced/paren group), which a bare
^{3/2} already attaches to correctly. Hand-simplified to
(1-x^{2})^{3/2}, which typesets identically.

This review also restores the repeated x= in the hyperbolic-substitution instructions, places prose variables and axes in math mode, and separates equations and boundary conditions into readable math spans.

